# Qorpera agent exit (E8c-2): the server name check of "only listed". qorpera-agent-exit.sh loads it with
# qorpera-agent-exit.nft in one transaction, and only while the kernel has nft_queue and nfnetlink_queue loaded
# already: the queue rule would make the kernel load nft_queue. Without both modules (on the nodes until Jonas says yes
# to them) "only listed" goes by address alone.
#
# An only_P chain sets ct mark 1 on the first packet of a port 443 flow to a listed address. Every packet of a flow
# marked 1, both ways, goes to queue 0, where qorpera-agent-exit-sni.py reads the machine's ClientHello. It lets packets
# on unchanged, or answers with a meta mark and runs this chain again (NF_REPEAT):
# - 0x80000001: the server acknowledged a ClientHello that names a listed server; the flow becomes 2 and is never
#   queued again;
# - 0x80000002: refused; the packet is refused with that mark (the logger reads it as name_not_listed), the flow
#   becomes 3 and every packet of it is dropped from then on.
# With no checker on queue 0 (it stopped, or restarts) the kernel drops the packets (no bypass): a flow being judged
# then is refused, never let through unread. The brake's marks are 1..0x7FFFFFFF, so bit 31 never meets them.
table inet qorpera_agent_exit {
	# After forward (priority filter), so it sees every packet forward accepted, established ones too.
	chain sni {
		type filter hook forward priority filter + 1; policy accept;
		ct mark 1 jump sni_judge
		ct mark 3 drop
	}

	chain sni_judge {
		meta mark 0x80000001 meta mark set 0 ct mark set 2 accept
		meta mark 0x80000002 ct mark set 3 counter name "refused_name" goto refuse
		queue num 0
	}
}
